<title>GREECE: GREEK WPI EDGES UP TO 2.6 PCT YR/YR IN MAY.</title>
<headline>GREEK WPI EDGES UP TO 2.6 PCT YR/YR IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek wholesale price inflation rose to 2.6 percent year-on-year in May from 2.5 percent in Arpil, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>Average inflation in January-May fell to 2.8 percent year-on-year from 6.7 percent and 9.4 percent in the same period in 1996 and 1995 respectively, it said.</p>
<p>    Wholesale Price Index     May 97     April 97     May 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 0.5%	 0.8%	  0.3%</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   2.6%	 2.5%	  6.9%</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	   888.7	 884.6	  866.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
